      ⍝ empty-other-axis regression: LO\B with a user-defined LO used to
      ⍝ hit an INDEX ERROR whenever B had a non-scanned axis of length 0
      ⍝ while the scanned axis itself had length >1 (the empty-B guard
      ⍝ was checked after, not before, the macro dispatch for a defined
      ⍝ LO). The scanned axis itself being 0 already worked (m_len==0
      ⍝ returns early); this exercises the "some *other* axis is 0" case.

      LO←{⍺+⍵}
      ⍴LO\(0 3⍴0)
0 3

      LO\(0 3⍴0)

      ⍴LO\(3 0⍴0)
3 0

      ⍝ ==================================

